.nh
.TH "PB-INBOX-APPROVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-inbox-approve - Approve an exact team file request


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb inbox approve <request-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Approve one pending team file request. The sender can then deliver exactly the files in the
request, no others. File names are checked against this computer's rules first, and a request
this system cannot store is refused before it is approved.

.PP
--generation is optional: without it the command uses the request's current generation. Pass it
to approve only if the request has not changed since you looked at it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected request generation (default: the request's current one)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for approve

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb inbox requests
  pb inbox approve request_abc123
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-inbox(1)\fP
